3909	PERF-SQL-QE-001-RC01	1	1	Missing or poorly designed indexes	Query performs full table scans instead of index seeks, requiring sequential reading of all rows	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	{"mysql": "`innodb_buffer_pool_size` undersizing causes excessive disk I/O; `sort_buffer_size` and `read_rnd_buffer_size` too small cause performance degradation; replication lag can mask slow query detection; query cache (MySQL 5.x) can sometimes harm performance", "oracle": "Incorrect `OPTIMIZER_MODE` setting (e.g., RULE vs CBO); system statistics not gathered via `DBMS_STATS`; unset `STATISTICS_LEVEL` prevents automatic statistics collection; undersized `db_cache_size` or `sga_target`; high `DB_FILE_MULTIBLOCK_READ_COUNT` without I/O subsystem support", "mariadb": "Specific InnoDB settings like `innodb_io_capacity` too low relative to hardware; `join_buffer_size` insufficient for BKA (batched key access) joins", "vertica": "Query optimizer chooses low-selectivity projections instead of focused projections; `GROUP BY HASH` triggered instead of `GROUP BY PIPELINE` due to incorrect projection sort order; lack of column encoding/compression increases I/O requirements", "sqlserver": "Automatic statistics update with synchronous mode (`AUTO_UPDATE_STATISTICS_ASYNC` OFF) blocks query execution; missing filtered indexes on partial predicates; `max_degree_of_parallelism (MAXDOP)` misconfiguration causes serial execution or excessive parallelism overhead; large memory grants cause memory pressure", "postgresql": "Check `log_min_duration_statement` setting; stale statistics require manual `ANALYZE` execution if autovacuum is disabled or cannot keep up; `work_mem` undersizing causes external sorts; dead rows accumulation from incomplete `VACUUM` operations bloats tables"}	\N	\N
