6011	SEC-SQL-PRI-002-RC06	147	6	Crash Dumps and Core Files	When a database process crashes (e.g., Segfault), it writes a memory dump (core file) to disk. These dumps contain fragments of RAM which often hold clear text PII and passwords from recent queries.	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	\N	\N	\N
