5995	SEC-SQL-PRI-001-RC01	146	1	Misunderstanding of "Encryption at Rest" (TDE)	Teams often enable Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) or disk-level encryption (e.g., AWS EBS encryption) and believe the data is secure. This protects physical drives but *automatically decrypts* data for any valid user or application connection, leaving PII exposed to SQL injection or rogue DBAs.	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	\N	\N	\N
5996	SEC-SQL-PRI-001-RC02	146	2	Searchability \\& Indexing Requirements	Applications often need to search, sort, or join on PII fields (e.g., "Find user by email"). Encrypting these columns (using randomized encryption) breaks indexing and search capability, so developers default to clear text to maintain performance.	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	\N	\N	\N
