6007	SEC-SQL-PRI-002-RC02	147	2	Unparameterized Queries (String Concatenation)	Developers build SQL queries using string concatenation (e.g., `query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE ssn = '" + ssn_var + "'"`). This sends the literal PII value to the database log. Parameterized queries (using `?` or `$1`) would only log the query structure, not the sensitive data.	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	\N	\N	\N
5997	SEC-SQL-PRI-001-RC03	146	3	Performance Overhead Fears	Developers avoid column-level encryption due to fears that decryption overhead will slow down high-throughput queries or increase CPU usage significantly.	\N	{mariadb,mysql,oracle,postgresql,sqlserver,vertica}	\N	\N	\N
