6148	PERF-VEC-QRY-002-RC01	475	1	Filter has low selectivity (high cardinality matches)	Filter condition matches most records (e.g., `status != deleted`). Pre-filter eliminates few candidates; vector search still operates on nearly full dataset.	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	{"milvus": "Payload index must be explicitly created with `create_payload_index()`. IVF/HNSW search uses `filter` parameter; query planner estimates filter selectivity to decide full-scan vs. index probe. Higher `nprobe` partially compensates for low filter selectivity but increases CPU overhead.", "qdrant": "Payload index on filtered fields essential. ACORN (Filter-Aware HNSW) automatically routes search to bypass disconnected graph nodes not matching filter. On-disk payload index available for large metadata; reduces memory but increases latency for frequently filtered fields.", "chromadb": "No native payload indexes; filtering is full-scan based. Workaround: pre-filter results in application layer before querying Chroma, or use external metadata store (PostgreSQL, Redis) for filtering.", "weaviate": "ACORN filter strategy (v1.27+) dramatically improves performance by constraining graph traversal during search. Pre-ACORN versions used post-filter only. Proper field indexing via `invertedIndex` critical.", "postgresql": "Pre-filters via `WHERE` clause use standard PostgreSQL query planner. `pg_stat_user_tables` tracks actual filter selectivity; planner learns over time. Explicit `ANALYZE` table updates statistics for better plans. Parallel sequential scans possible with `max_parallel_workers_per_gather`."}	\N	\N
