6241	PERF-VEC-ING-001-RC03	481	3	Transaction Commit Overhead	Databases using Write-Ahead Logs (WAL) must fsync to disk for durability; doing this per vector triggers excessive disk I/O operations per second (IOPS).	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	{"milvus": "Small inserts create \\"growing segments\\" that fragment memory. Frequent flushing of small segments triggers aggressive compaction, spiking CPU usage on DataNodes.", "qdrant": "The optimizer runs background tasks to merge segments; single inserts can trigger these tasks too frequently if `vacuum_min_vector_number` is not tuned, leading to write amplification.", "chromadb": "Relying on standard `add` calls with single documents performs poorly due to SQLite's transaction management; persistent storage writes become the bottleneck.", "weaviate": "Object creation has a fixed overhead (~2ms). Failing to use the `/batch` endpoint results in a linear performance degradation of 10-100x compared to batched imports.", "postgresql": "Single `INSERT` statements incur full transaction overhead. Using `COPY` or multi-row `INSERT` is mandatory for performance; otherwise, WAL writes bottleneck the disk."}	\N	\N
