6224	PERF-VEC-QRY-007-RC01	480	1	Vector normalization mismatch	Vectors indexed with L2 normalization but query not normalized (or vice versa). Normalized vector has unit norm; unnormalized vector has arbitrary norm; distance calculations yield wrong ranking.	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	{"milvus": "Metric specified at collection creation via `metric_type` parameter. Supported: L2, IP (inner product), COSINE. Per-query metric override not supported; index metric used for all queries. Normalization not automatic; user responsible for L2 normalization before ingestion.", "qdrant": "Metric specified per-collection; dot product, cosine, Euclidean supported. Per-query metric override not supported. Qdrant automatically normalizes vectors for cosine; user should normalize for dot product if needed.", "chromadb": "Metric specified at collection creation. Supported: l2, ip (inner product), cosine. Per-query override not supported. Normalization depends on FAISS backend implementation; generally automatic for cosine.", "weaviate": "Metric specified per-class in schema (`\\"vectorDistanceMetric\\": \\"cosine\\"`). HNSW graph built with specified metric. Per-query override possible via `distance` parameter in GraphQL query. Normalization automatic; user input vectors automatically normalized.", "postgresql": "Metric specified via operator type at index creation (vector_l2_ops, vector_cosine_ops, vector_ip_ops). Per-query metric override possible via `<->` (L2), `<=>` (cosine), `<#>` (inner product) operators. Query vector not normalized automatically; user responsible for normalization before query."}	\N	\N
