6589	HLTH-VEC-MNT-002-RC20	506	20	Replication lag of schema changes	Primary’s schema update is ahead of replicas; clients routed to replicas encounter old dimensions or index definitions. Vendor-Specific Notes: - Pinecone: Vector dimension is fixed per index; any change requires deleting and recreating the index with the new dimension. - Milvus: Vector field `dim` is immutable; you must drop/recreate the collection (and re-ingest data) to change dimensions. - Qdrant: Collection config declares vector size; inserts must match exactly, or they are rejected. - Weaviate: Class vectorizer and dimensions are tied to schema; changing vectorizer often implies creating a new class or reimporting data. - pgvector: Column types like `vector(1536)` enforce exact dimensions; ALTER TABLE is required for a dimension change. - MongoDB Atlas Vector Search: Vector index definitions include `dimensions`; all vectors must match that length. - Elasticsearch/OpenSearch: Dense vector fields must use the dimension declared in the mapping; changing requires a new index and reindex. - Redis VSS: RediSearch vector index DIM setting must match all stored vectors; mismatches cause index errors.	\N	{chromadb,milvus,qdrant,weaviate}	\N	\N	\N
